{\pard\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fntnamaut Chorus 1\par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fntnamaut It is well, with my soul,\par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fntnamaut It is well,\par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fntnamaut It is well, with my soul. \par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fntnamaut Verse 1\par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fntnamaut When peace like a river,\par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fntnamaut Attendeth my way,\par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fntnamaut When sorrows,\par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fntnamaut Like sea billows roll;\par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fntnamaut Whatever my lot,\par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fntnamaut Thou hast taught me to say,\par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fntnamaut "It is well,\par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fntnamaut It is well, with my soul." \par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fntnamaut Verse 2\par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fntnamaut Though Satan should buffet,\par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fntnamaut Tho' trials should come,\par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fntnamaut Let this blest assurance control;\par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fntnamaut That Christ has regarded\par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fntnamaut My helpless estate,\par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fntnamaut And hath shed His own blood\par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fntnamaut For my soul. \par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fntnamaut Verse 3\par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fntnamaut My sin, O the bliss\par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fntnamaut Of this glorious tho't,\par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fntnamaut My sin not in part\par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fntnamaut But the whole\par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fntnamaut Is nailed to the cross\par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fntnamaut And I bear it no more.\par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fntnamaut Praise the Lord,\par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fntnamaut Praise the Lord, O my soul! \par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fntnamaut Verse 4\par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fntnamaut O, Lord haste the day\par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fntnamaut When my faith shall be sight,\par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fntnamaut The clouds be rolled back\par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fntnamaut As a scroll;\par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fntnamaut The trump shall resound\par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fntnamaut And the Lord shall descend,\par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fntnamaut "Even so" it is well\par
\li0\fi0\ri0\sb0\sl\sa0 \plain\f1\fntnamaut With my soul.}
